verdict_summary: >
  The plan maps every spec requirement to exactly one task, and all three rows are
  confirmed. It is fit to execute only as a skeleton. Each task restates its
  requirement without adding specificity. The "empty" and non-Ada gaps from the
  spec carry through unchanged, the test assertions are unnamed, and no file or
  verification targets exist. These are specificity gaps, not coverage gaps.
  Resolve them before an executor starts (P0 and P1 below).

coverage_assessment:
  method: >
    Read the spec and the proposed tasklist directly and checked each matrix row
    against them. Linkage is by explicit R-ID in the task heading, so the
    match_method "exact" claim holds for ID linkage. It does not hold for semantic
    completeness, which is covered under gaps.
  rows:
    - requirement_id: R-001
      task_id: T-101
      verdict: confirmed
      reasoning: "T-101 heading carries R-001; body targets the greeting but does not restate the exact string (G-01)."
      citations:
        - {file: SPEC, line: 5, quote: "## R-001 Greeting"}
        - {file: SPEC, line: 6, quote: "The greet function MUST return the exact string Hello, Ada! for Ada."}
        - {file: PROPOSED, line: 3, quote: "## T-101 R-001"}
        - {file: PROPOSED, line: 4, quote: "Implement greet(name) returning the required greeting."}
        - {file: MATRIX, line: 11, quote: "{requirement_id: R-001, source: parsed, span: \"spec.md:5-7\", matched_task_ids: [T-101], match_method: exact}"}
      matrix_check: "Span 5-7 consistent; line 7 blank before R-002 heading at line 8."
    - requirement_id: R-002
      task_id: T-102
      verdict: confirmed
      reasoning: "T-102 references R-002 and names ValueError; does not define 'empty' (G-02)."
      citations:
        - {file: SPEC, line: 8, quote: "## R-002 Empty input"}
        - {file: SPEC, line: 9, quote: "The greet function MUST reject an empty name with ValueError."}
        - {file: PROPOSED, line: 6, quote: "## T-102 R-002"}
        - {file: PROPOSED, line: 7, quote: "Reject an empty name using ValueError."}
        - {file: MATRIX, line: 12, quote: "{requirement_id: R-002, source: parsed, span: \"spec.md:8-10\", matched_task_ids: [T-102], match_method: exact}"}
      matrix_check: "Span 8-10 consistent; line 10 blank before R-003 heading at line 11."
    - requirement_id: R-003
      task_id: T-103
      verdict: confirmed
      reasoning: "T-103 references R-003 and names both scenarios; assertion content unspecified (G-03)."
      citations:
        - {file: SPEC, line: 11, quote: "## R-003 Evidence"}
        - {file: SPEC, line: 12, quote: "Tests MUST exercise the ordinary greeting and empty-input rejection."}
        - {file: PROPOSED, line: 9, quote: "## T-103 R-003"}
        - {file: PROPOSED, line: 10, quote: "Add ordinary and empty-name test cases."}
        - {file: MATRIX, line: 13, quote: "{requirement_id: R-003, source: parsed, span: \"spec.md:11-12\", matched_task_ids: [T-103], match_method: exact}"}
      matrix_check: "Span 11-12 consistent; file ends at line 12."
  matrix_summary_check:
    parsed_requirements_in_spec: 3
    tasks_in_proposed: 3
    coverage_pct_confirmed: 1.0
    unmapped_requirements: []
    citations:
      - {file: MATRIX, line: 18, quote: "coverage_pct: 1.0"}
      - {file: MATRIX, line: 20, quote: "unmapped_requirements: []"}
      - {file: MATRIX, line: 24, quote: "S_dev_density: 0.0"}
    matrix_drop_claim_check: "Inferred candidates at spec.md:6, :9, :12 correctly dropped as body lines of R-001..R-003."
